\fBwithPreferredRuntimeScheme(value, arg)\fR
Rewrites the provided specifier or URL so it uses the preferred runtime scheme. When `options.url === true`, the `://` delimiter is assumed. Otherwise `:` is used.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIvalue\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ url?: boolean, scheme?: string }; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring\fR
.TP
\fBruntimeOrigin(bundleIdentifier, arg)\fR
Builds a runtime origin string (e.g., `oro://com.example.app`).
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIbundleIdentifier\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ scheme?: string }; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring\fR
.TP
\fBnormalizeRuntimeScheme(scheme)\fR
Normalizes a scheme string (with/without the trailing colon) to the runtime value. Returns an empty string for unrecognised schemes.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIscheme\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring\fR
